# "{2}: If this Equipment isn't a creature, it becomes a 0/0 Construct Hero artifact creature with flying and 'This creature gets +1/+1 for each artifact you control' until
# end of turn." On turn 1 the Armor attaches to Bot1's Ornithopter (2/3). On turn 3 Bot1 pays {2}: the Armor becomes a creature, so it is an Equipment creature and
# becomes unattached (CR 301.5c, 704.5p) - the Ornithopter is a 0/2 again - and, with the six artifacts Bot1 controls (the Armor, four Moxen and the Ornithopter),
# a 6/6 Construct Hero Equipment artifact creature with flying. The second {2} paid finds the "if this Equipment isn't a creature" untrue as it resolves and does
# nothing (it is still 6/6, one Hero, nothing doubled). It attacks, having been under Bot1's control since turn 1, and deals 6: Bot2 is at 14. On turn 4 it is
# only an artifact again (CR 514.2). Bot2's two Moxen are artifacts too, but "you control" leaves them out of the count: it is 6, not 8.

